<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Denote the input token dimension as <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expert functions.</span> We study expert functions <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, which are realized by standard feedforward neural networks employing the ReLU activation function. Specifically, each expert map <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is represented as a composition of affine transformations and ReLU nonlinearities:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(x;\theta)=f_{L}\circ\sigma\circ f_{L-1}\circ\cdots\circ\sigma\circ f_{1}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}(x;\theta)=f_{L}\circ\sigma\circ f_{L-1}\circ\cdots\circ\sigma\circ f_{1}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each affine layer is defined by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle f_{i}(x)=xW_{i}+b_{i},\quad\text{for }i=1,\dots,L." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{i}(x)=xW_{i}+b_{i},\quad\text{for }i=1,\dots,L.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the ReLU activation function, applied component-wise, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the full set of learnable parameters. The weight matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{i-1}\times n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{i-1}\times n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and bias vector <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> parameterize the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer, where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{0}=n_{L}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{0}=n_{L}=d</annotation></semantics></math> is the input and output dimensions, respectively. We have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta\in\prod_{i=1}^{L}(\mathbb{R}^{n_{i-1}\times n_{i}}\times\mathbb{R}^{n_{i}})=\mathbb{R}^{e},~\text{ where }~e=\sum_{i=1}^{L}(n_{i-1}n_{i}+n_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>e</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta\in\prod_{i=1}^{L}(\mathbb{R}^{n_{i-1}\times n_{i}}\times\mathbb{R}^{n_{i}})=\mathbb{R}^{e},~\text{ where }~e=\sum_{i=1}^{L}(n_{i-1}n_{i}+n_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Define the <span id="A1.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">weight space of expert functions</span> as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Theta=\prod_{i=1}^{L}\left(\mathbb{R}^{n_{i-1}\times n_{i}}\times\mathbb{R}^{n_{i}}\right)=\mathbb{R}^{e}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>e</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Theta=\prod_{i=1}^{L}\left(\mathbb{R}^{n_{i-1}\times n_{i}}\times\mathbb{R}^{n_{i}}\right)=\mathbb{R}^{e}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dense Mixture-of-Experts.</span> Given a positive integer <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> representing the number of experts, a <em id="A1.SS1.p1.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mixture-of-Experts with Dense gating</em> (MoE) is defined as the function: <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}~\colon~\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}~\colon~\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">The function <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is parameterized as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(x;\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(x;\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> where</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi=\Big(\big(W_{i},b_{i}\big),\theta_{i}\Big)_{i=1,\ldots,n}\in\Big(\big(\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}\big)\times\Theta\Big)^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi=\Big(\big(W_{i},b_{i}\big),\theta_{i}\Big)_{i=1,\ldots,n}\in\Big(\big(\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}\big)\times\Theta\Big)^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Denote the <span id="A1.SS1.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">weight space of a Mixture of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> Experts</span> as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi(n)=\Big(\big(\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}\big)\times\Theta\Big)^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi(n)=\Big(\big(\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}\big)\times\Theta\Big)^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Varying the number of experts leads to a Mixture-of-Experts weight space that spans across expert sets of different sizes, denoted by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi=\bigsqcup_{n=1}^{\infty}\Phi(n)=\bigsqcup_{n=1}^{\infty}\Big(\big(\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}\big)\times\Theta\Big)^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi=\bigsqcup_{n=1}^{\infty}\Phi(n)=\bigsqcup_{n=1}^{\infty}\Big(\big(\mathbb{R}^{D}\times\mathbb{R}\big)\times\Theta\Big)^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sparse Mixture-of-Experts. </span> Given a positive integer <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Top}\text{-}k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Top</mtext><mtext>-</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Top}\text{-}k</annotation></semantics></math> map is defined by: for any vector <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Top-}k(z)=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Top-}k(z)=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are the indices corresponding to the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> largest components of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. In the event of ties, we select smaller indices first. Using this, a <span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse gating</span> (SMoE) is the function <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\sum_{i\in T(x)}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i\in T(x)}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\sum_{i\in T(x)}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i\in T(x)}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(x)=T\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\text{Top-}k\Big(\big(W_{i}x+b_{i}\big)_{i=1}^{n}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(x)=T\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\text{Top-}k\Big(\big(W_{i}x+b_{i}\big)_{i=1}^{n}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The weight space for the Sparse Mixture-of-Experts is identical to that of the Dense Mixture-of-Experts, as the inclusion of the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Top-}k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Top-}k</annotation></semantics></math> operator does not introduce any additional trainable parameters. However, the SMoE function <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is generally discontinuous, primarily due to the non-smooth nature of the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Top-}k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Top-}k</annotation></semantics></math> selection–particularly in scenarios where multiple experts share identical gating scores (i.e., ties occur). To circumvent this issue and ensure well-defined behavior, we restrict our analysis to a subset of the input space <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> where the top <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> gating scores are uniquely determined without ambiguity. In particular, for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\in(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\in(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we define the subset of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the gating scores of all experts are pairwise distinct, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\text{ are pairwise distinct}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> are pairwise distinct</mtext></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\text{ are pairwise distinct}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">We provide one result characterizing the structure of this domain, and another result describing the behavior of the SMoE map when it is restricted to inputs within this domain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is an open and dense subset of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}~\text{ is pairwise distinct for all }i=1,\ldots,n\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mtext> is pairwise distinct for all </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}~\text{ is pairwise distinct for all }i=1,\ldots,n\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigcap_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}\neq W_{j}x+b_{j}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigcap_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}\neq W_{j}x+b_{j}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigcap_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}\left(\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}=W_{j}x+b_{j}\right\}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigcap_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}\left(\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}=W_{j}x+b_{j}\right\}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that, the set</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}=W_{j}x+b_{j}\right\}=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\left(W_{i}-W_{j}\right)x=b_{j}-b_{i}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}=W_{j}x+b_{j}\right\}=\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\left(W_{i}-W_{j}\right)x=b_{j}-b_{i}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">is either a hyperplane (when <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}\neq W_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}\neq W_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>) or empty (when <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}=W_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=W_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}\neq b_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}\neq b_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>). In both scenarios, its complement in <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> forms an open and dense subset. By Equation (<a href="#A1.Ex1" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), and using the fact that a finite intersection of open and dense subsets in <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> remains open and dense, it follows that the set <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left({W_{i},b_{i}}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left({W_{i},b_{i}}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is itself open and dense in <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, then the SMoE map <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, as given in Equation (<a href="#A1.E21" title="In A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), is continuous over the domain <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega\left(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega\left(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of this set, there exists an open neighborhood <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset\Omega\left(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset\Omega\left(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Top-}k\left(\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\text{Top-}k\left(\left(W_{i}y+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Top-}k\left(\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\text{Top-}k\left(\left(W_{i}y+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in U</annotation></semantics></math>. This condition ensures that the sparse gating mechanism defined in Equation (<a href="#A1.E21" title="In A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) remains fixed within <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and consequently, the SMoE map is continuous on the domain <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Propositions <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition A.1. ‣ A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition A.2. ‣ A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> serve as essential building blocks in the proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Group Action on Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts </h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define the group <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G(n)=\left(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}\right)\times\text{S}_{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G(n)=\left(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}\right)\times\text{S}_{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is the direct product of the additive groups <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the symmetric group <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> elements. Each element <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written in the form</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau),\quad\text{where }c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d},~c_{b}\in\mathbb{R},~\text{and }\tau\in\text{S}_{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau),\quad\text{where }c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d},~c_{b}\in\mathbb{R},~\text{and }\tau\in\text{S}_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The group <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> acts on the weight space <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(n)</annotation></semantics></math> as follows: for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in\Phi(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in\Phi(n)</annotation></semantics></math> given as in Equation (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), the action is defined by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g\phi\coloneqq\left(W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W},\;b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b},\;\theta_{\tau(i)}\right)_{i=1,\ldots,n}\in\Phi(n)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g\phi\coloneqq\left(W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W},\;b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b},\;\theta_{\tau(i)}\right)_{i=1,\ldots,n}\in\Phi(n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">This group action preserves the functionality of both the MoE and SMoE maps. The invariance arises from two key properties: the permutation invariance of the summation operator, and the translation invariance of the softmax function. We begin by establishing a result that characterizes the invariance of MoE maps under this group action.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weight space invariance of Mixture-of-Experts)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The MoE map <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-invariance under the action of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> on its weight space, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;g\phi)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;g\phi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. For all <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}(x;g\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}(x;g\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{\left(W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}\right)x+\left(b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}\right)\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{\tau(i)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{\left(W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}\right)x+\left(b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}\right)\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{\tau(i)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{\tau(i)}x+b_{\tau(i)}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{\tau(i)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{\tau(i)}x+b_{\tau(i)}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{\tau(i)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{D}(x;\theta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{D}(x;\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the proposition is proven.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The analysis of the SMoE architecture requires additional assumptions due to the inherent discontinuity of the Top-<math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selection operator. In what follows, we show that the SMoE map, when restricted to an appropriate subset of its domain, remains invariant under the group action of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weight space invariance of Sparse Mixture-of-Experts)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the SMoE map as defined in Equation (<a href="#A1.E21" title="In A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), assume that the pairs <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i},b_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i},b_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the set <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under the group action of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\Omega\left(g\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\Omega\left(g\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, the SMoE map, restricted to</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math>-invariance under the action of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> on its weight space, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\theta)=\mathcal{S}(\cdot;g\theta)~~\text{ on }~~\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> on </mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\theta)=\mathcal{S}(\cdot;g\theta)~~\text{ on }~~\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. We first verify that the group action preserves the set <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}~\text{ is pairwise distinct for all }i=1,\ldots,n\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mtext> is pairwise distinct for all </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~W_{i}x+b_{i}~\text{ is pairwise distinct for all }i=1,\ldots,n\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\left(W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}\right)x+\left(b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}\right)~\text{ is pairwise distinct for all }i=1,\ldots,n\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow><mtext> is pairwise distinct for all </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\left(W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}\right)x+\left(b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}\right)~\text{ is pairwise distinct for all }i=1,\ldots,n\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(g\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(g\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle gT(x)=\text{Top-}k\bigg(\Big(\left(W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}\right)x+\left(b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}\right)\Big)_{i=1}^{n}\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle gT(x)=\text{Top-}k\bigg(\Big(\left(W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}\right)x+\left(b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}\right)\Big)_{i=1}^{n}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">For all <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="gT(x)=\tau(T(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">gT(x)=\tau(T(x))</annotation></semantics></math>. The desired invariance result for the SMoE map then follows by applying the same reasoning as in Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition A.3 (Weight space invariance of Mixture-of-Experts). ‣ A.2 Group Action on Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the group action on Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) models is formally introduced in Equation (<a href="#A1.E22" title="In A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), it does not fully capture all symmetries inherent to these architectures. In particular, each expert network possesses internal neuron permutations that preserve its functional behavior–a well-documented property in the literature on neural networks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">77</a>, <a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">82</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. Nonetheless, since the distinguishing feature of MoE models is their input-dependent gating function, our focus centers on the symmetries associated with the gate itself, treating expert-level invariances as part of a well-established theoretical foundation.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>A Structural Property of Neural Networks with ReLU Activation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">polytope</span> is a geometric entity bounded by flat surfaces, which can be either finite (bounded) or infinite (unbounded) in extent. We define the notion of <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">local affineness</span> as follows: a function <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be locally affine if there exists a partition of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> into a finite set of polytopes such that on each polytope, the function <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> agrees with an affine transformation from <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the term <em id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">local affineness</em> may take on different interpretations in other contexts, its usage here is unambiguous within the scope of this work.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We examine the local affineness property in ReLU neural networks. Consider a feedforward neural network <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{n_{0}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{n_{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{n_{0}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{n_{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> constructed from affine maps interleaved with ReLU activations, given by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f=f_{L}\circ\sigma\circ f_{L-1}\circ\cdots\circ\sigma\circ f_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{L}\circ\sigma\circ f_{L-1}\circ\cdots\circ\sigma\circ f_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where each map <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{i-1}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{i-1}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is affine and has the form <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(x)=W_{i}x+b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(x)=W_{i}x+b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the ReLU function applied elementwise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The combination of these affine transformations and ReLU activations partitions the domain <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> into finitely many convex polytopes. On each such region, the activation status of the ReLU units–whether they transmit their input or suppress it to zero–remains fixed. Consequently, the network reduces to a simpler form in which each ReLU behaves either as the identity or the zero function. Given that both ReLU and affine maps are piecewise linear and closed under composition, the overall function <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is affine within each activation region.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, the network satisfies the following property:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(x)=A_{i}x+b_{i},\quad\text{for all }x\in P_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(x)=A_{i}x+b_{i},\quad\text{for all }x\in P_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the domain is partitioned into polytopes <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> define the affine transformation active within region <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the boundary of the polytope <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the set</p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}\setminus\bigcup_{i=1}^{m}\partial P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}\setminus\bigcup_{i=1}^{m}\partial P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">is open and dense in <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>; in other words, the union of the interiors of the polytopes covers a set that is both open and dense.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now consider a finite collection of ReLU networks <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the intersection of finitely many open dense subsets is itself open and dense, there exists a subset <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for every point <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a neighborhood around <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> on which all functions <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> act as affine maps.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>A Technical Lemma on Holomorphic Functions in <math id="A2.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A function <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon\mathbb{C}^{n}\rightarrow\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon\mathbb{C}^{n}\rightarrow\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">holomorphic on <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></span> if it is complex differentiable at every point in <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. A function is called <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">meromorphic on <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math></span> if it can be locally written as a quotient of two holomorphic functions, where the denominator is not identically zero. The collection of all holomorphic functions on <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> forms an integral domain, denoted by <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the set of meromorphic functions on <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a field, denoted by <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is the field of fractions of the integral domain <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}[x]=\mathbb{C}[x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}[x]=\mathbb{C}[x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the polynomial ring in <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> complex variables, and let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}(x)=\mathbb{C}(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}(x)=\mathbb{C}(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the corresponding field of rational functions. Then <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}[x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}[x]</annotation></semantics></math> is a subring of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and remains an integral domain, while <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a subfield of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and represents the field of fractions of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}[x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}[x]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any polynomial <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathbb{C}[x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathbb{C}[x]</annotation></semantics></math>, the exponential <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> defines a holomorphic function on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{p}\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{p}\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}(x)\subset\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}(x)\subset\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can view <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> as a vector space over <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. The following lemma addresses the linear independence of exponential functions of polynomials in this vector space setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\ldots,p_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\ldots,p_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be polynomials in <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}[x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}[x]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}-p_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}-p_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonconstant whenever <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the functions <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{p_{1}},\ldots,e^{p_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{p_{1}},\ldots,e^{p_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, viewed as elements of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, are linearly independent over <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed by induction on <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. The base case <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math> is immediate, since <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{p}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{p}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for any polynomial <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume the result holds for any smaller number of exponentials. Consider polynomials <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},\ldots,r_{N}\in\mathbb{C}[x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},\ldots,r_{N}\in\mathbb{C}[x]</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{1}\cdot e^{p_{1}}+\cdots+r_{N}\cdot e^{p_{N}}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{1}\cdot e^{p_{1}}+\cdots+r_{N}\cdot e^{p_{N}}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We aim to prove that all <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose not; then at least one <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonzero. Without loss of generality, assume <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{N}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{N}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Dividing through by <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{N}\cdot e^{p_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{N}\cdot e^{p_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{r_{1}}{r_{N}}\cdot e^{p_{1}-p_{N}}+\cdots+\frac{r_{N-1}}{r_{N}}\cdot e^{p_{N-1}-p_{N}}+1=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{r_{1}}{r_{N}}\cdot e^{p_{1}-p_{N}}+\cdots+\frac{r_{N-1}}{r_{N}}\cdot e^{p_{N-1}-p_{N}}+1=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating both sides with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{N-1}\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\left(\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\right)+\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(p_{j}-p_{N})\right)\cdot e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{N-1}\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\left(\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\right)+\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(p_{j}-p_{N})\right)\cdot e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Note that each term</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\left(\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\right)+\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(p_{j}-p_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\left(\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\right)+\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(p_{j}-p_{N})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">belongs to <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, the polynomials <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}-p_{N},\ldots,p_{N-1}-p_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}-p_{N},\ldots,p_{N-1}-p_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct and nonconstant. Thus, by the induction hypothesis, the exponentials <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> are linearly independent over <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,N-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, from equation (<a href="#A2.E41" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 A Technical Lemma on Holomorphic Functions in ℂ^𝑛 ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), we must have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\left(\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\right)+\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(p_{j}-p_{N})=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\left(\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\right)+\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}(p_{j}-p_{N})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,N-1</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\left(\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}\right)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{i}}\left(\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}\right)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, for each <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,N-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the function</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}=c_{j}\in\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{r_{j}}{r_{N}}\cdot e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}=c_{j}\in\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">must be constant. If <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then both <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}=\frac{c_{j}r_{N}}{r_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}=\frac{c_{j}r_{N}}{r_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> must hold. But this forces <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{p_{j}-p_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be constant, which contradicts the assumption that <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}-p_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}-p_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonconstant. Thus, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,N-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging back into equation (<a href="#A2.E40" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 A Technical Lemma on Holomorphic Functions in ℂ^𝑛 ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) gives a contradiction, as <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, all <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This lemma plays a key role and will be applied repeatedly in the proofs of Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following result establishes the equivalence between two sets of weights that define the same MoE map. Certain assumptions are introduced for technical reasons, and their justification is provided in Remark <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Remark B.6 (Rationale behind the assumptions in Theorem ). ‣ Step 5. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi,\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi,\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> define the same MoE function, i.e. <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that the following conditions hold:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:22pt;">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Both </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> consist of pairwise distinct functions;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Both </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}-W_{j}\}_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}-W_{j}\}_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}^{\prime}-W_{j}^{\prime}\}_{1\leq i&lt;j&lt;n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}^{\prime}-W_{j}^{\prime}\}_{1\leq i&lt;j&lt;n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> consist of pairwise distinct vector of </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and there exists <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}^{\prime}=W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}^{\prime}=W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}^{\prime}=b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}^{\prime}=b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})=\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{\tau(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})=\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{\tau(i)})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To enhance clarity, we begin by outlining the main steps of the proof at a high level:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first expand the equality <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and introduce simplified notation to streamline the subsequent derivations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We then observe that each expert function can be locally characterized as an affine map.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we prove that <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and establish the existence of a permutation <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and a transformation <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{W}</annotation></semantics></math> with the required properties.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We proceed to verify the equivalence between the two sets of experts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we show that a transformation <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the necessary conditions can be constructed.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We now proceed with the detailed derivations and justifications corresponding to each of the five steps above.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1. </h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)=\sum_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta^{\prime}_{i}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)=\sum_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta^{\prime}_{i}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{i}(\cdot)=\mathcal{E}\left(\cdot;\theta_{i}\right),~~~\text{ and }~~~\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(\cdot)=\mathcal{E}\left(\cdot;\theta^{\prime}_{i}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.157em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0.990em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{i}(\cdot)=\mathcal{E}\left(\cdot;\theta_{i}\right),~~~\text{ and }~~~\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(\cdot)=\mathcal{E}\left(\cdot;\theta^{\prime}_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By expanding the softmax terms in Equation (<a href="#A2.E46" title="In Step 1. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>), we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\dfrac{e^{W_{i}x+b_{i}}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}e^{W_{j}x+b_{j}}}\cdot\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}\dfrac{e^{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{W^{\prime}_{j}x+b^{\prime}_{j}}}\cdot\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\dfrac{e^{W_{i}x+b_{i}}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n}e^{W_{j}x+b_{j}}}\cdot\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}\dfrac{e^{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}}}{\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{W^{\prime}_{j}x+b^{\prime}_{j}}}\cdot\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Multiplying both sides by the respective denominators yields</p>
<table id="A2.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{W^{\prime}_{j}x+b^{\prime}_{j}}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}e^{W_{i}x+b_{i}}\cdot\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)\right)=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}e^{W_{j}x+b_{j}}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}}\cdot\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{W^{\prime}_{j}x+b^{\prime}_{j}}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}e^{W_{i}x+b_{i}}\cdot\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)\right)=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}e^{W_{j}x+b_{j}}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}}\cdot\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which can be rewritten as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{\left(W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}\right)x+\left(b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}\right)}\cdot\left(\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)-\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}(x)\right)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{\left(W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}\right)x+\left(b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}\right)}\cdot\left(\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)-\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}(x)\right)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2. </h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since each function <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally affine, it follows from the result in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 A Structural Property of Neural Networks with ReLU Activation ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> that there exists a dense open subset <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that: for any point <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, one can find an open neighborhood <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> on which all functions <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are affine. Consequently, each of these functions agrees with a polynomial on <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, there exists a family of open sets <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U_{k}\}_{k\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U_{k}\}_{k\in I}</annotation></semantics></math> covering <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega=\bigcup_{k\in I}U_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega=\bigcup_{k\in I}U_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and for each set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=U_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=U_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in this cover, there exist polynomials <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{U,i},p^{\prime}_{U,j}\in\mathbb{R}[x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{U,i},p^{\prime}_{U,j}\in\mathbb{R}[x]</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)=p_{U,i}(x),~~~~\text{ and }~~~~\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}(x)=p^{\prime}_{U,j}(x)~~\text{ for all }x\in U." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.487em">,</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1.32em;" width="1.32em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)=p_{U,i}(x),~~~~\text{ and }~~~~\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}(x)=p^{\prime}_{U,j}(x)~~\text{ for all }x\in U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting into Equation (<a href="#A2.E50" title="In Step 1. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>) yields:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{\left(W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}\right)x+\left(b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}\right)}\cdot\left(p_{U,i}(x)-p^{\prime}_{U,j}(x)\right)=0~~\text{ for all }x\in U." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{\left(W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}\right)x+\left(b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}\right)}\cdot\left(p_{U,i}(x)-p^{\prime}_{U,j}(x)\right)=0~~\text{ for all }x\in U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Observe that the expression on the left-hand side above defines a holomorphic function. By the Identity Theorem for Holomorphic Functions (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">74</a>]</cite>), we conclude that:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{\left(W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}\right)x+\left(b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}\right)}\cdot\left(p_{U,i}(x)-p^{\prime}_{U,j}(x)\right)=0~~\text{ for all }x\in\mathbb{C}^{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}e^{\left(W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}\right)x+\left(b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}\right)}\cdot\left(p_{U,i}(x)-p^{\prime}_{U,j}(x)\right)=0~~\text{ for all }x\in\mathbb{C}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3. </h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">According to Assumption 2, the sets <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are composed of mutually distinct elements. As a result, there exists a direction</p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\|x\|_{2}=1\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\|x\|_{2}=1\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">such that the projected values <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}\alpha\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}\alpha\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W^{\prime}_{j}\alpha\}_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W^{\prime}_{j}\alpha\}_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are comprised of <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> distinct real numbers, respectively. Without loss of generality, we may relabel the indices so that:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha&lt;W_{2}\alpha&lt;\ldots&lt;W_{n}\alpha~~\text{ and }~~W^{\prime}_{1}\alpha&lt;W^{\prime}_{2}\alpha&lt;\ldots&lt;W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha&lt;W_{2}\alpha&lt;\ldots&lt;W_{n}\alpha~~\text{ and }~~W^{\prime}_{1}\alpha&lt;W^{\prime}_{2}\alpha&lt;\ldots&lt;W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, observe that the problem setting and the preceding equations are invariant under translations of the form <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}_{j}\mapstochar\rightarrow W^{\prime}_{j}+c_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}_{j}\mapstochar\rightarrow W^{\prime}_{j}+c_{W}</annotation></semantics></math> for a constant vector <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we can assume without loss of generality that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}=W^{\prime}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=W^{\prime}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this assumption, we aim to demonstrate that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. Toward that goal, we begin by showing that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,\min\{n,n^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,\min\{n,n^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> using mathematical induction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Base case. </span> By assumption, we have <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}=W^{\prime}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=W^{\prime}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the base case holds trivially.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Auxiliary step for induction. </span> For every index pair <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\neq(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\neq(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the inequality:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{1}\alpha&lt;W_{i}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{j}\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{1}\alpha&lt;W_{i}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{j}\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the sum <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\neq(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\neq(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying Equation (<a href="#A2.E54" title="In Step 2. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>) in conjunction with Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 A Technical Lemma on Holomorphic Functions in ℂ^𝑛 ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, we conclude that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inductive step. </span> Assume that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> holds for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is an integer such that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;k\leq\min\{n,n^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;k\leq\min\{n,n^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose, for contradiction, that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}\neq W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}\neq W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. We analyze the terms <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}+W^{\prime}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}+W^{\prime}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under our assumption, these two quantities must differ. Without loss of generality, we may assume that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{k}\alpha\leq W_{k}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{1}\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{k}\alpha\leq W_{k}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{1}\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all index pairs <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{k}\alpha\leq W_{k}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{1}\alpha\leq W_{i}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{j}\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{k}\alpha\leq W_{k}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{1}\alpha\leq W_{i}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{j}\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Equality holds if and only if <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)=(k,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)=(k,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, since <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}+W^{\prime}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}+W^{\prime}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct, it follows that <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{k}\alpha\leq W_{i}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{j}\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{k}\alpha\leq W_{i}\alpha+W^{\prime}_{j}\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Equality occurs only when <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)=(1,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)=(1,k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is distinct from <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\neq(1,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\neq(1,k)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math>, we claim that <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> does not equal <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose, for contradiction, that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}=W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}=W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for some pair <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by the induction hypothesis,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}=W^{\prime}_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}=W^{\prime}_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Rearranging terms, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}-W^{\prime}_{j}=W^{\prime}_{i}-W^{\prime}_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}-W^{\prime}_{j}=W^{\prime}_{i}-W^{\prime}_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which contradicts the assumption that all such differences are pairwise distinct, since <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,j)\neq(i,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,j)\neq(i,k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">These observations collectively show that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\neq(1,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\neq(1,k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying Equation (<a href="#A2.E54" title="In Step 2. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>) together with Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 A Technical Lemma on Holomorphic Functions in ℂ^𝑛 ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, we conclude that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Additionally, from Equation (<a href="#A2.E58" title="In Step 3. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>), we already have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p^{\prime}_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p^{\prime}_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">This implies that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{1}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{1}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Since this holds for every open set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> in the covering <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U_{k}\}_{k\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U_{k}\}_{k\in I}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{1}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{1}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is dense in <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and each <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, we conclude that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{1}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{1}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> on all of <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. This contradicts the assumption that the <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> functions are pairwise distinct. Therefore, our initial assumption must be false, and we conclude that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}=W_{k}+W^{\prime}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{k}=W_{k}+W^{\prime}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}=W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}=W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Conclusion.</span> By induction, we have established that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,\min\{n,n^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,\min\{n,n^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. It remains to show that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose, for contradiction, that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&lt;n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&lt;n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the sum <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that this quantity is distinct from every <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\neq(1,n^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\neq(1,n^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume otherwise, that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}=W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}=W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">for some pair <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\neq(1,n^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\neq(1,n^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the inductive assumption that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce</p>
<table id="A2.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}+W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}=W^{\prime}_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}+W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}=W^{\prime}_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.3" class="ltx_p">which implies</p>
<table id="A2.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}-W^{\prime}_{j}=W^{\prime}_{i}-W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}-W^{\prime}_{j}=W^{\prime}_{i}-W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.4" class="ltx_p">This leads to a contradiction, as it violates the assumption that the differences <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}_{i}-W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}_{i}-W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct. Hence, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}+W^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> must be distinct from all other sums <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\neq(1,n^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\neq(1,n^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by Equation (<a href="#A2.E54" title="In Step 2. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>) and Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 A Technical Lemma on Holomorphic Functions in ℂ^𝑛 ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, it follows that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,n^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,n^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.5" class="ltx_p">In addition, from Equation (<a href="#A2.E58" title="In Step 3. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>), we already know that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p^{\prime}_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,n^{\prime}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p^{\prime}_{U,1}=p^{\prime}_{U,n^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.6" class="ltx_p">Consequently, we obtain <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{1}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{1}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Since this holds on every open set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> in the covering <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U_{k}\}_{k\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U_{k}\}_{k\in I}</annotation></semantics></math>, it extends to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, and by continuity, to all of <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. This contradicts the assumption that the expert functions <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct. Therefore, our assumption must be false, and we conclude that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, the reordering of indices and the translation applied to the set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W^{\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> throughout the argument confirm the existence of a permutation <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\textup{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\textup{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and a translation vector <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now establish that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. From <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3</span>, we already have that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=W^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all indices in this range. Consider any pair <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>. If it holds that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}=W_{i^{\prime}}+W^{\prime}_{j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}=W_{i^{\prime}}+W^{\prime}_{j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> must be either <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,i)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, this implies that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is distinct from <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{j}+W^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{j}+W^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,k)\neq(i,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,k)\neq(i,i)</annotation></semantics></math>. Invoking Equation (<a href="#A2.E54" title="In Step 2. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>) together with Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 A Technical Lemma on Holomorphic Functions in ℂ^𝑛 ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{U,i}=p^{\prime}_{U,i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{U,i}=p^{\prime}_{U,i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This argument parallels that used in <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3</span>, and applying the same reasoning, we conclude that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since this holds for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, the result follows.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 5.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to prove the existence of a constant <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{b}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{b}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{i}+c_{b}\quad\text{for all }i=1,\ldots,n." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{i}+c_{b}\quad\text{for all }i=1,\ldots,n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Recall from <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4</span> that if <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}=W_{i^{\prime}}+W^{\prime}_{j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}=W_{i^{\prime}}+W^{\prime}_{j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then it must be that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})=(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})=(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,i)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this structural property, along with Equation (<a href="#A2.E50" title="In Step 1. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>), Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ B.2 A Technical Lemma on Holomorphic Functions in ℂ^𝑛 ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, and the identity <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> established in <span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4</span>, we derive the following equality:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{\left(W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}\right)x+\left(b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}\right)}\cdot\left(\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)-\mathcal{E}_{j}(x)\right)+e^{\left(W_{j}+W^{\prime}_{i}\right)x+\left(b_{j}+b^{\prime}_{i}\right)}\cdot\left(\mathcal{E}_{j}(x)-\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)\right)=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{\left(W_{i}+W^{\prime}_{j}\right)x+\left(b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}\right)}\cdot\left(\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)-\mathcal{E}_{j}(x)\right)+e^{\left(W_{j}+W^{\prime}_{i}\right)x+\left(b_{j}+b^{\prime}_{i}\right)}\cdot\left(\mathcal{E}_{j}(x)-\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)\right)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">valid for all index pairs <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}\neq\mathcal{E}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}\neq\mathcal{E}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a point <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}(x_{0})\neq\mathcal{E}_{j}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}(x_{0})\neq\mathcal{E}_{j}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> into Equation (<a href="#A2.E74" title="In Step 5. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>) and simplifying by factoring out the common nonzero difference, we find:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e^{b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}}=e^{b_{j}+b^{\prime}_{i}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e^{b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}}=e^{b_{j}+b^{\prime}_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which implies</p>
<table id="A2.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}=b_{j}+b^{\prime}_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{i}+b^{\prime}_{j}=b_{j}+b^{\prime}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and hence</p>
<table id="A2.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{i}-b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{j}-b^{\prime}_{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{i}-b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{j}-b^{\prime}_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This shows that the difference <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}-b^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}-b^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> remains constant for all <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Letting <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{b}:=b^{\prime}_{1}-b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{b}:=b^{\prime}_{1}-b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{i}+c_{b}\quad\text{for all }i=1,\ldots,n." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{i}+c_{b}\quad\text{for all }i=1,\ldots,n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.7" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rationale behind the assumptions in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In modeling architectures, it is important that the symmetry group arises from the structure of the model itself rather than from specific, possibly degenerate, parameter choices. That is, the symmetry group should act globally and consistently across the entire weight space. This requirement motivates the following conditions in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>:</p>
<ol id="A2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:22pt;">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> consist of pairwise distinct functions;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}-W_{j}\}_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}-W_{j}\}_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}^{\prime}-W_{j}^{\prime}\}_{1\leq i&lt;j&lt;n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}^{\prime}-W_{j}^{\prime}\}_{1\leq i&lt;j&lt;n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> consist of pairwise distinct vector of <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now elaborate on the purpose of these assumptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumption 1. </span> If this condition is violated–for instance, if two experts compute the same function and are assigned identical gating values–then permuting these experts leaves the model output unchanged. Such permutations introduce additional, non-essential elements into the symmetry group, which we refer to as spurious symmetries. These do not correspond to genuine structural invariances but rather arise from degenerate parameter settings that represent singular points in the model’s parameter space.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumption 2. </span> Assumption 2 addresses a more nuanced issue: it rules out cases where linear dependencies among gating weight vectors may cause multiple experts to exhibit indistinguishable gating behavior. Although such situations may not be as immediately intuitive as those excluded by Assumption 1, they too can artificially enlarge the symmetry group beyond its intended form. To illustrate this, we present an explicit example. Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}=3</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider parameter configurations <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</p>
<ul id="A2.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}=W^{\prime}_{1}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=W^{\prime}_{1}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}=W^{\prime}_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}=W^{\prime}_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{3}=W^{\prime}_{3}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{3}=W^{\prime}_{3}=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The parameters <math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1},\theta_{2},\theta_{3},\theta_{1}^{\prime},\theta_{2}^{\prime},\theta_{3}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1},\theta_{2},\theta_{3},\theta_{1}^{\prime},\theta_{2}^{\prime},\theta_{3}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are chosen so that all six experts are constant functions. Let us define:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.EGx75.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{llll}\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{1})&amp;=A_{1},&amp;\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{1}^{\prime})&amp;=A_{2},\\
\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{2})&amp;=B_{1},&amp;\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{2}^{\prime})&amp;=B_{2},\\
\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{3})&amp;=C_{1},&amp;\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{3}^{\prime})&amp;=C_{2}.\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="7.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{llll}\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{1})&amp;=A_{1},&amp;\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{1}^{\prime})&amp;=A_{2},\\
\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{2})&amp;=B_{1},&amp;\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{2}^{\prime})&amp;=B_{2},\\
\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{3})&amp;=C_{1},&amp;\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{3}^{\prime})&amp;=C_{2}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now select the biases <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j},B_{j},C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j},B_{j},C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the models satisfy <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, even though there exists no transformation as described in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> that maps <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to ensure that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{e^{-x+b_{1}}}{e^{-x+b_{1}}+e^{b_{2}}+e^{x+b_{3}}}\cdot A_{1}+\dfrac{e^{b_{2}}}{e^{-x+b_{1}}+e^{b_{2}}+e^{x+b_{3}}}\cdot B_{1}+\dfrac{e^{x+b_{3}}}{e^{-x+b_{1}}+e^{b_{2}}+e^{x+b_{3}}}\cdot C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{e^{-x+b_{1}}}{e^{-x+b_{1}}+e^{b_{2}}+e^{x+b_{3}}}\cdot A_{1}+\dfrac{e^{b_{2}}}{e^{-x+b_{1}}+e^{b_{2}}+e^{x+b_{3}}}\cdot B_{1}+\dfrac{e^{x+b_{3}}}{e^{-x+b_{1}}+e^{b_{2}}+e^{x+b_{3}}}\cdot C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=~" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=~</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dfrac{e^{-x+b^{\prime}_{1}}}{e^{-x+b^{\prime}_{1}}+e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}+e^{x+b^{\prime}_{3}}}\cdot A_{2}+\dfrac{e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}}{e^{-x+b^{\prime}_{1}}+e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}+e^{x+b^{\prime}_{3}}}\cdot B_{2}+\dfrac{e^{x+b^{\prime}_{3}}}{e^{-x+b^{\prime}_{1}}+e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}+e^{x+b^{\prime}_{3}}}\cdot C_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dfrac{e^{-x+b^{\prime}_{1}}}{e^{-x+b^{\prime}_{1}}+e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}+e^{x+b^{\prime}_{3}}}\cdot A_{2}+\dfrac{e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}}{e^{-x+b^{\prime}_{1}}+e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}+e^{x+b^{\prime}_{3}}}\cdot B_{2}+\dfrac{e^{x+b^{\prime}_{3}}}{e^{-x+b^{\prime}_{1}}+e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}+e^{x+b^{\prime}_{3}}}\cdot C_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For convenience, we introduce the following shorthand:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.EGx77.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{llll}e^{b_{1}}&amp;=X_{1},&amp;e^{b^{\prime}_{1}}&amp;=X_{2},\\
e^{b_{2}}&amp;=Y_{1},&amp;e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}&amp;=Y_{2},\\
e^{b_{3}}&amp;=Z_{1},&amp;e^{b^{\prime}_{3}}&amp;=Z_{2}.\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="7.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{llll}e^{b_{1}}&amp;=X_{1},&amp;e^{b^{\prime}_{1}}&amp;=X_{2},\\
e^{b_{2}}&amp;=Y_{1},&amp;e^{b^{\prime}_{2}}&amp;=Y_{2},\\
e^{b_{3}}&amp;=Z_{1},&amp;e^{b^{\prime}_{3}}&amp;=Z_{2}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.2" class="ltx_p">With this notation, Equation (<a href="#A2.Ex10" title="In Remark B.6 (Rationale behind the assumptions in Theorem ). ‣ Step 5. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a>) becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.0pt\dfrac{e^{-x}X_{1}}{e^{-x}X_{1}+Y_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}}\cdot A_{1}+\dfrac{Y_{1}}{e^{-x}X_{1}+Y_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}}\cdot B_{1}+\dfrac{e^{x}Z_{1}}{e^{-x}X_{1}+Y_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}}\cdot C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.0pt\dfrac{e^{-x}X_{1}}{e^{-x}X_{1}+Y_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}}\cdot A_{1}+\dfrac{Y_{1}}{e^{-x}X_{1}+Y_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}}\cdot B_{1}+\dfrac{e^{x}Z_{1}}{e^{-x}X_{1}+Y_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}}\cdot C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.0pt\dfrac{e^{-x}X_{2}}{e^{-x}X_{2}+Y_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}}\cdot A_{2}+\dfrac{Y_{2}}{e^{-x}X_{2}+Y_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}}\cdot B_{2}+\dfrac{e^{x}Z_{2}}{e^{-x}X_{2}+Y_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}}\cdot C_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.0pt\dfrac{e^{-x}X_{2}}{e^{-x}X_{2}+Y_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}}\cdot A_{2}+\dfrac{Y_{2}}{e^{-x}X_{2}+Y_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}}\cdot B_{2}+\dfrac{e^{x}Z_{2}}{e^{-x}X_{2}+Y_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}}\cdot C_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.3" class="ltx_p">which is equivalent to:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(e^{-x}X_{1}A_{1}+Y_{1}B_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}C_{1}\right)\left(e^{-x}X_{2}+Y_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(e^{-x}X_{1}A_{1}+Y_{1}B_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}C_{1}\right)\left(e^{-x}X_{2}+Y_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 100.0pt=\left(e^{-x}X_{2}A_{2}+Y_{2}B_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}C_{2}\right)\left(e^{-x}X_{1}+Y_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="10.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 100.0pt=\left(e^{-x}X_{2}A_{2}+Y_{2}B_{2}+e^{x}Z_{2}C_{2}\right)\left(e^{-x}X_{1}+Y_{1}+e^{x}Z_{1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.4" class="ltx_p">By equating the coefficients of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-2x},e^{-x},1,e^{x},e^{2x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-2x},e^{-x},1,e^{x},e^{2x}</annotation></semantics></math>, we derive the following system:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.EGx80.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lllll}e^{-2x}&amp;\colon&amp;X_{1}X_{2}A_{1}&amp;=&amp;X_{1}X_{2}A_{2},\\
e^{2x}&amp;\colon&amp;Z_{1}Z_{2}C_{1}&amp;=&amp;Z_{1}Z_{2}C_{2},\\
e^{x}&amp;\colon&amp;Y_{1}Z_{2}B_{1}+Z_{1}Y_{2}C_{1}&amp;=&amp;Y_{1}Z_{2}C_{2}+Z_{1}Y_{2}B_{2},\\
e^{-x}&amp;\colon&amp;Y_{1}X_{2}B_{1}+X_{1}Y_{2}A_{1}&amp;=&amp;Y_{1}X_{2}A_{2}+X_{1}Y_{2}B_{2},\\
1&amp;\colon&amp;X_{1}Z_{2}A_{1}+Z_{1}X_{2}C_{1}+Y_{1}Y_{2}B_{1}&amp;=&amp;X_{1}Z_{2}C_{2}+Z_{1}X_{2}A_{2}+Y_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}.\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="7.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lllll}e^{-2x}&amp;\colon&amp;X_{1}X_{2}A_{1}&amp;=&amp;X_{1}X_{2}A_{2},\\
e^{2x}&amp;\colon&amp;Z_{1}Z_{2}C_{1}&amp;=&amp;Z_{1}Z_{2}C_{2},\\
e^{x}&amp;\colon&amp;Y_{1}Z_{2}B_{1}+Z_{1}Y_{2}C_{1}&amp;=&amp;Y_{1}Z_{2}C_{2}+Z_{1}Y_{2}B_{2},\\
e^{-x}&amp;\colon&amp;Y_{1}X_{2}B_{1}+X_{1}Y_{2}A_{1}&amp;=&amp;Y_{1}X_{2}A_{2}+X_{1}Y_{2}B_{2},\\
1&amp;\colon&amp;X_{1}Z_{2}A_{1}+Z_{1}X_{2}C_{1}+Y_{1}Y_{2}B_{1}&amp;=&amp;X_{1}Z_{2}C_{2}+Z_{1}X_{2}A_{2}+Y_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.5" class="ltx_p">Setting <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}=A_{2}=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}=A_{2}=A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=C_{2}=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=C_{2}=C</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the equations involving <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-2x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-2x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{2x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{2x}</annotation></semantics></math> automatically. Removing those, we simplify the system to:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.EGx81.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lllll}e^{x}&amp;\colon&amp;Y_{1}Z_{2}B_{1}+Z_{1}Y_{2}C&amp;=&amp;Y_{1}Z_{2}C+Z_{1}Y_{2}B_{2},\\
e^{-x}&amp;\colon&amp;Y_{1}X_{2}B_{1}+X_{1}Y_{2}A&amp;=&amp;Y_{1}X_{2}A+X_{1}Y_{2}B_{2},\\
1&amp;\colon&amp;X_{1}Z_{2}A+Z_{1}X_{2}C+Y_{1}Y_{2}B_{1}&amp;=&amp;X_{1}Z_{2}C+Z_{1}X_{2}A+Y_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}.\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="7.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>:</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lllll}e^{x}&amp;\colon&amp;Y_{1}Z_{2}B_{1}+Z_{1}Y_{2}C&amp;=&amp;Y_{1}Z_{2}C+Z_{1}Y_{2}B_{2},\\
e^{-x}&amp;\colon&amp;Y_{1}X_{2}B_{1}+X_{1}Y_{2}A&amp;=&amp;Y_{1}X_{2}A+X_{1}Y_{2}B_{2},\\
1&amp;\colon&amp;X_{1}Z_{2}A+Z_{1}X_{2}C+Y_{1}Y_{2}B_{1}&amp;=&amp;X_{1}Z_{2}C+Z_{1}X_{2}A+Y_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.6" class="ltx_p">Solving the equations for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, assuming <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}Y_{2}\neq Y_{1}Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}Y_{2}\neq Y_{1}Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}Y_{2}\neq Y_{1}X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}Y_{2}\neq Y_{1}X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.EGx82.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lll}A&amp;=&amp;\dfrac{X_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2}B_{1}}{X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2}},\\
C&amp;=&amp;\dfrac{Z_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2}B_{1}}{Z_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2}}.\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="15.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>A</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>C</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lll}A&amp;=&amp;\dfrac{X_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2}B_{1}}{X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2}},\\
C&amp;=&amp;\dfrac{Z_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2}B_{1}}{Z_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2}}.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.7" class="ltx_p">Substituting into the constant term equation in (<a href="#A2.EGx81" title="Remark B.6 (Rationale behind the assumptions in Theorem ). ‣ Step 5. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>) gives:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{1}Y_{2}(B_{1}-B_{2})=(C-A)(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{1}Y_{2}(B_{1}-B_{2})=(C-A)(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.8" class="ltx_p">Now computing <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A-C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A-C</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A-C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A-C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{X_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2}B_{1}}{X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2}}-\dfrac{Z_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2}B_{1}}{Z_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{X_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2}B_{1}}{X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2}}-\dfrac{Z_{1}Y_{2}B_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2}B_{1}}{Z_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\dfrac{Y_{1}Y_{2}(B_{1}-B_{2})(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2})}{(X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2})(Z_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\dfrac{Y_{1}Y_{2}(B_{1}-B_{2})(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2})}{(X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2})(Z_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.9" class="ltx_p">Plugging into Equation (<a href="#A2.E98" title="In Remark B.6 (Rationale behind the assumptions in Theorem ). ‣ Step 5. ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">98</span></a>), we find:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{1}Y_{2}(B_{1}-B_{2})=-\dfrac{Y_{1}Y_{2}(B_{1}-B_{2})(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2})}{(X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2})(Z_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2})}(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{1}Y_{2}(B_{1}-B_{2})=-\dfrac{Y_{1}Y_{2}(B_{1}-B_{2})(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2})}{(X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2})(Z_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}Z_{2})}(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.10" class="ltx_p">Assuming <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}\neq B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}\neq B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1}Y_{2}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1}Y_{2}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we divide both sides to obtain:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2})(Y_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}Y_{2})=(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2})^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(X_{1}Y_{2}-Y_{1}X_{2})(Y_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}Y_{2})=(X_{1}Z_{2}-Z_{1}X_{2})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.11" class="ltx_p">While this equation can be solved in general, it suffices to exhibit a concrete solution. Consider:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.EGx87.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lll}(X_{1},X_{2})&amp;=&amp;(1,2),\\
(Y_{1},Y_{2})&amp;=&amp;(3,5),\\
(Z_{1},Z_{2})&amp;=&amp;(2,3).\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="7.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lll}(X_{1},X_{2})&amp;=&amp;(1,2),\\
(Y_{1},Y_{2})&amp;=&amp;(3,5),\\
(Z_{1},Z_{2})&amp;=&amp;(2,3).\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.12" class="ltx_p">With these values, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> may be freely chosen. These assignments define parameter configurations <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{D}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, yet no transformation described in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> maps <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Strongly Distinctness Property</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following definition formalizes the notion of <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">strong distinctness</span>, which will be used in the statement of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Strongly distinct)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two functions <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g\colon X\rightarrow Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g\colon X\rightarrow Y</annotation></semantics></math> are said to be <span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">strongly distinct</span> if the set <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x\in X~\colon~f(x)\neq g(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x\in X~\colon~f(x)\neq g(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math> is dense in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present several examples to illustrate the concept of strong distinctness.</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two distinct polynomials on <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are strongly distinct.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two distinct holomorphic functions are strongly distinct.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, two distinct locally affine functions are not necessarily strongly distinct. For instance:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1},f_{2}\colon\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1},f_{2}\colon\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{1}(x)=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }x&lt;0,\\
x&amp;\text{if }x\geq 0,\end{cases}\hskip 50.0ptf_{2}(x)=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:5em;" width="5em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{1}(x)=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }x&lt;0,\\
x&amp;\text{if }x\geq 0,\end{cases}\hskip 50.0ptf_{2}(x)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are strongly distinct.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},g_{2}\colon\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},g_{2}\colon\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{1}(x)=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }x&lt;0,\\
x&amp;\text{if }x\geq 0,\end{cases}\hskip 50.0ptg_{2}(x)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:5em;" width="5em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{1}(x)=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }x&lt;0,\\
x&amp;\text{if }x\geq 0,\end{cases}\hskip 50.0ptg_{2}(x)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct but not strongly distinct, since they coincide on <math id="A3.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\infty,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\infty,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now define a certain class of subsets of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given</p>
<table id="A3.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\in\left(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}\right)^{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\in\left(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}\right)^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">we define the set</p>
<table id="A3.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\coloneqq\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\text{ are pairwise distinct}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.608em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> are pairwise distinct</mtext></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\coloneqq\left\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}~\colon~\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\text{ are pairwise distinct}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following result provides a sufficient condition on the gating weights under which the Top-<math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> operator is capable of selecting any subset of <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> experts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the collection <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the condition that the set <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W^{(G,i-1)}-W^{(G,i)}\}_{i=2}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W^{(G,i-1)}-W^{(G,i)}\}_{i=2}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is linearly independent in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for every subset <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\subseteq\{1,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\subseteq\{1,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a point <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{Top-}k\left(\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\mathcal{A}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{Top-}k\left(\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\mathcal{A}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, assume <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{1,\ldots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{1,\ldots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math>. To prove the existence of <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{Top-}k\left(\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\{1,\ldots,k\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{Top-}k\left(\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\{1,\ldots,k\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">it suffices to find <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}x+b_{1}&gt;W_{2}x+b_{2}&gt;\cdots&gt;W_{n}x+b_{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}x+b_{1}&gt;W_{2}x+b_{2}&gt;\cdots&gt;W_{n}x+b_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">We can strengthen this to require:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.EGx95.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.EGx95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lcl}(W_{1}x+b_{1})-(W_{2}x+b_{2})&amp;=&amp;1,\\
(W_{2}x+b_{2})-(W_{3}x+b_{3})&amp;=&amp;1,\\
&amp;\vdots&amp;\\
(W_{n-1}x+b_{n-1})-(W_{n}x+b_{n})&amp;=&amp;1.\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="7.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lcl}(W_{1}x+b_{1})-(W_{2}x+b_{2})&amp;=&amp;1,\\
(W_{2}x+b_{2})-(W_{3}x+b_{3})&amp;=&amp;1,\\
&amp;\vdots&amp;\\
(W_{n-1}x+b_{n-1})-(W_{n}x+b_{n})&amp;=&amp;1.\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">This is equivalent to the following system of linear equations:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.EGx96.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.EGx96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lcl}(W_{1}-W_{2})x&amp;=&amp;1-(b_{1}-b_{2}),\\
(W_{2}-W_{3})x&amp;=&amp;1-(b_{2}-b_{3}),\\
&amp;\vdots&amp;\\
(W_{n-1}-W_{n})x&amp;=&amp;1-(b_{n-1}-b_{n}).\end{array}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="7.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{array}[]{lcl}(W_{1}-W_{2})x&amp;=&amp;1-(b_{1}-b_{2}),\\
(W_{2}-W_{3})x&amp;=&amp;1-(b_{2}-b_{3}),\\
&amp;\vdots&amp;\\
(W_{n-1}-W_{n})x&amp;=&amp;1-(b_{n-1}-b_{n}).\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since the vectors <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i-1}-W_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i-1}-W_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are linearly independent by assumption, this system has a unique solution. Hence, there exists <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying Equation (<a href="#A3.EGx96" title="Proof. ‣ C.1 Strongly Distinctness Property ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition C.3. ‣ C.1 Strongly Distinctness Property ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> will be invoked in the proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>. A justification for the linear independence assumption is provided in Remark <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem8" title="Remark C.8 (Rationale behind the assumptions in Theorem ). ‣ Step 4. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We establish a functional equivalence theorem for the Sparse Mixture-of-Experts (SMoE) architecture, in parallel with the result for MoE given in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>. However, our analysis is limited to the case <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, as the <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> setting leads to singularities that disrupt the general structure of equivalence. A detailed explanation for this exclusion is provided in Remark <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem9" title="Remark C.9 (The case of 𝑘=1). ‣ Step 4. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi,\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi,\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> define the same SMoE function, i.e. <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that the following conditions hold:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:22pt;">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Both </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> consist of pairwise strongly distinct functions;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Both </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i-1}-W_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i-1}-W_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i-1}^{\prime}-W^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i-1}^{\prime}-W^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are linear independent subsets of </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and there exists <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=(c_{W},c_{b},\tau)\in G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}^{\prime}=W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}^{\prime}=W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}^{\prime}=b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}^{\prime}=b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{i}^{\prime})=\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{\tau(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{i}^{\prime})=\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{\tau(i)})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega(\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(i)\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(i)\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Before presenting the proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, we begin with two remarks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and there exist <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\textup{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\textup{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{b}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{b}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{i}=W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W},\quad b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{i}=W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W},\quad b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(120)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then the two sets <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i},b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i},b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> coincide. Furthermore, for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in this set, the condition <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(i)\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(i)\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> holds if and only if <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is easy to verify that Assumption 2 in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a> implies Assumption 2 in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To enhance clarity, we begin by outlining the main steps of the proof at a high level:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Formulate the identity <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly and introduce simplified notation to streamline the presentation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Partition the input space into regions where the <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Top-}k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Top-}k</annotation></semantics></math> operator selects the same index set, and within which all expert functions are affine.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Demonstrate the desired equivalence for a fixed subset of experts. The core technique is to invoke the MoE equivalence result given in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Generalize the argument to establish the equivalence across all experts.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now proceed with the detailed derivation and proofs for each of the outlined steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1. </h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi)=\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=~" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=~</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E121.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}})}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}})}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta^{\prime}_{i}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}})}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}})}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta^{\prime}_{i}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. To simplify notation, define</p>
<table id="A3.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{i}(\cdot)=\mathcal{E}\left(\cdot;\theta_{i}\right),~~\text{ and }~~\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(\cdot)=\mathcal{E}\left(\cdot;\theta^{\prime}_{i}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{i}(\cdot)=\mathcal{E}\left(\cdot;\theta_{i}\right),~~\text{ and }~~\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(\cdot)=\mathcal{E}\left(\cdot;\theta^{\prime}_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using this notation, we can rewrite Equation (<a href="#A3.Ex14" title="In Step 1. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">121</span></a>) more compactly as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=~" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=~</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E123.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}})}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}})}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}})}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i\in\textup{Top-}k((W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}})}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2. </h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by highlighting two key observations:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption 2 guarantees that the parameter pairs <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct for <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, and likewise, <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{W^{\prime}_{i},b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{W^{\prime}_{i},b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct for <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition A.1. ‣ A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, the set</p>
<table id="A3.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega_{1}=\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cap\Omega\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i},b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega_{1}=\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)\cap\Omega\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i},b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I4.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is open and dense in <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the values <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct. Moreover, for each <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an open neighborhood around <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in which both Top-<math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selections remain fixed.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the analysis in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 A Structural Property of Neural Networks with ReLU Activation ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, there exists a set <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{2}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{2}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, also open and dense, such that for every <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, all expert functions <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are affine in a neighborhood of <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Taking the intersection <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega=\Omega_{1}\cap\Omega_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega=\Omega_{1}\cap\Omega_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain a set that is still open and dense. Within <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, both the Top-<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selections and the expert functions remain locally constant and affine, respectively. Consequently, there exists a collection of open sets <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{U_{i}\}_{i\in I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{U_{i}\}_{i\in I}</annotation></semantics></math> that cover <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega=\bigcup_{i\in I}U_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega=\bigcup_{i\in I}U_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and on each <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the expert functions <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are affine, and the Top-<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selections do not vary.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3. </h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary open set from the cover described in Equation (<a href="#A3.E125" title="In Step 2. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">125</span></a>). Without loss of generality, we may relabel the indices such that both Top-<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> maps are constantly equal to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math> throughout <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this reindexing, Equation (<a href="#A3.Ex15" title="In Step 1. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">123</span></a>) simplifies to</p>
<table id="A3.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{k}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{k}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{k}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W_{i}x+b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{k}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 80.0pt=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{k}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x)\quad\text{for all }x\in U." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="8.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 80.0pt=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\left(\left\{W^{\prime}_{i}x+b^{\prime}_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{k}\right)\cdot\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x)\quad\text{for all }x\in U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">According to Assumption 1, the expert functions <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are strongly distinct, which implies that they remain distinct on the open set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. The same conclusion applies to the functions <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the assumptions of Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> are satisfied on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and Equation (<a href="#A3.Ex16" title="In Step 3. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">126</span></a>) falls within its scope. As a consequence, there exist constants <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{b}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{b}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, up to reindexing, we have for all <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,k</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{i}=W_{i}+c_{W},\quad b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{i}+c_{b}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{i}=W_{i}+c_{W},\quad b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{i}+c_{b},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and furthermore, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4. </h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any index <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{3,4,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{3,4,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we invoke Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition C.3. ‣ C.1 Strongly Distinctness Property ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> to select an open set <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> from the cover in Equation (<a href="#A3.E125" title="In Step 2. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">125</span></a>) such that both indices <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> appear in <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(V_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(V_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Restricting Equation (<a href="#A3.Ex15" title="In Step 1. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">123</span></a>) to <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, we conclude that there exist indices <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t_{1},s_{1}\leq n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t_{1},s_{1}\leq n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}-W_{m}=W^{\prime}_{t_{1}}-W^{\prime}_{s_{1}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}-W_{m}=W^{\prime}_{t_{1}}-W^{\prime}_{s_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(128)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the same reasoning with indices <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t_{2},s_{2}\leq n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t_{2},s_{2}\leq n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{2}-W_{m}=W^{\prime}_{t_{2}}-W^{\prime}_{s_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{2}-W_{m}=W^{\prime}_{t_{2}}-W^{\prime}_{s_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(129)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Subtracting Equation (<a href="#A3.E129" title="In Step 4. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">129</span></a>) from Equation (<a href="#A3.E128" title="In Step 4. ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">128</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A3.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}-W^{\prime}_{2}=W_{1}-W_{2}=(W_{1}-W_{m})-(W_{2}-W_{m})=(W^{\prime}_{t_{1}}-W^{\prime}_{s_{1}})-(W^{\prime}_{t_{2}}-W^{\prime}_{s_{2}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{1}-W^{\prime}_{2}=W_{1}-W_{2}=(W_{1}-W_{m})-(W_{2}-W_{m})=(W^{\prime}_{t_{1}}-W^{\prime}_{s_{1}})-(W^{\prime}_{t_{2}}-W^{\prime}_{s_{2}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(130)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Due to the linear independence guaranteed by Assumption 2, this identity can only hold if <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{2}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{2}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}=s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}=s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denoting this shared index by <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(m)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(m)=s_{1}=s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(m)=s_{1}=s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we then have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1}-W_{m}=W^{\prime}_{1}-W^{\prime}_{\tau(m)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1}-W_{m}=W^{\prime}_{1}-W^{\prime}_{\tau(m)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(131)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which implies</p>
<table id="A3.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{\tau(m)}-W_{m}=W^{\prime}_{1}-W_{1}=c_{W}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{\tau(m)}-W_{m}=W^{\prime}_{1}-W_{1}=c_{W}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(132)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Similarly, we deduce</p>
<table id="A3.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b^{\prime}_{\tau(m)}-b_{m}=b^{\prime}_{1}-b_{1}=c_{b}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b^{\prime}_{\tau(m)}-b_{m}=b^{\prime}_{1}-b_{1}=c_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(133)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> ranges over <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{3,4,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{3,4,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding values of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(m)</annotation></semantics></math> must be distinct. If not, suppose that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(m)=\tau(m^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(m)=\tau(m^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, which would imply</p>
<table id="A3.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{m}-W_{m^{\prime}}=W^{\prime}_{\tau(m)}-W^{\prime}_{\tau(m^{\prime})}=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{m}-W_{m^{\prime}}=W^{\prime}_{\tau(m)}-W^{\prime}_{\tau(m^{\prime})}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(134)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">contradicting Assumption 3.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Applying a symmetric argument to the parameters of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(\cdot;\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, there exists a permutation <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{i}=W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W},\quad b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W^{\prime}_{i}=W_{\tau(i)}+c_{W},\quad b^{\prime}_{i}=b_{\tau(i)}+c_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(135)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the analysis above shows that for any <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(i)\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(i)\in\textup{Top-}k((W_{i}x+b_{i})_{i=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>–i.e., when index <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is selected by the Top-<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> operator in <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>–we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\tau(i)}(x)=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\tau(i)}(x)=\mathcal{E}^{\prime}_{i}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(136)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark C.7</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a> is conceptually analogous to Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, it is crucial to recognize that establishing the result for SMoE involves substantially greater technical complexity. The main challenge arises from the Top-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> operator, which introduces discontinuities by dynamically changing the subset of active experts in a manner that depends intricately on the input. This input-dependent behavior complicates the analysis and makes the theoretical treatment significantly more delicate.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark C.8</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rationale behind the assumptions in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by restating the two assumptions made in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I5" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:22pt;">
<li id="A3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both <math id="A3.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{\prime})\}_{i=1}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> consist of pairwise strongly distinct functions;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both <math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i-1}-W_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i-1}-W_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{i-1}^{\prime}-W^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{i-1}^{\prime}-W^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are linear independent subsets of <math id="A3.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These assumptions are strictly stronger than those required in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem B.5 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating). ‣ B.3 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ Appendix B Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Dense Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>. We now discuss their necessity and implications in greater detail.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumption 1.</span> This condition arises primarily from the behavior of the Top-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> operator, which induces input-dependent expert selection. As a result, the functional contribution of an expert is restricted to regions where it is actively selected by the gating mechanism. Outside these regions, the expert can behave arbitrarily without influencing the output. Therefore, if the experts are merely pairwise distinct–rather than pairwise strongly distinct–it becomes possible for different sets of expert functions to yield identical overall behavior when restricted to their respective activation domains. This ambiguity underscores the necessity of strong distinctness to ensure functional identifiability in the SMoE setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assumption 2.</span> In practice, the number of experts <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is typically much smaller than the input (token) dimension <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, the collections <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W^{(G,i-1)}-W_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W^{(G,i-1)}-W_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W^{\prime(G,i-1)}-W^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W^{\prime(G,i-1)}-W^{\prime}_{i}\}_{i=2}^{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are generically linearly independent. However, when linear dependence arises, it can prevent certain expert pairs from ever being simultaneously selected by the gating mechanism across all possible inputs. This limitation introduces singular symmetries: different parameter configurations that yield functionally identical outputs but cannot be related via the equivalence structure defined in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate this phenomenon concretely, consider an example with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{1},\mathcal{E}_{2},\mathcal{E}_{3},\mathcal{E}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{1},\mathcal{E}_{2},\mathcal{E}_{3},\mathcal{E}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> denote arbitrary expert functions. Define two SMoE models <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose gating logits are <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-2x,-x,x,2x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-2x,-x,x,2x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-3x,-2x,2x,3x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-3x,-2x,2x,3x)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. The resulting functions take the form:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx114" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}_{1}(x)=\begin{cases}\operatorname{softmax}_{1}(-2x,-x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{1}(x)+\operatorname{softmax}_{2}(-2x,-x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{2}(x)&amp;\text{if }x&lt;0,\\
\operatorname{softmax}_{1}(x,2x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{3}(x)+\operatorname{softmax}_{2}(x,2x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{4}(x)&amp;\text{if }x&gt;0,\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}_{1}(x)=\begin{cases}\operatorname{softmax}_{1}(-2x,-x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{1}(x)+\operatorname{softmax}_{2}(-2x,-x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{2}(x)&amp;\text{if }x&lt;0,\\
\operatorname{softmax}_{1}(x,2x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{3}(x)+\operatorname{softmax}_{2}(x,2x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{4}(x)&amp;\text{if }x&gt;0,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(137)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p6.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A3.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}_{2}(x)=\begin{cases}\operatorname{softmax}_{1}(-3x,-2x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{1}(x)+\operatorname{softmax}_{2}(-3x,-2x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{2}(x)&amp;\text{if }x&lt;0,\\
\operatorname{softmax}_{1}(2x,3x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{3}(x)+\operatorname{softmax}_{2}(2x,3x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{4}(x)&amp;\text{if }x&gt;0.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}_{2}(x)=\begin{cases}\operatorname{softmax}_{1}(-3x,-2x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{1}(x)+\operatorname{softmax}_{2}(-3x,-2x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{2}(x)&amp;\text{if }x&lt;0,\\
\operatorname{softmax}_{1}(2x,3x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{3}(x)+\operatorname{softmax}_{2}(2x,3x)\cdot\mathcal{E}_{4}(x)&amp;\text{if }x&gt;0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(138)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p7.1" class="ltx_p">It is easy to verify that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{1}(x)=\mathcal{S}_{2}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{1}(x)=\mathcal{S}_{2}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the gating logits are pairwise distinct and the Top-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selections remain constant. However, no transformation of the form specified in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem C.4 (Functional equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating). ‣ C.2 Functional Equivalence in Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ Appendix C Results on Mixture-of-Experts with Sparse Gating ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a> maps one configuration to the other. This demonstrates how singular symmetries can arise in the SMoE architecture, even when functional outputs coincide on an open dense subset of the input domain.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark C.9</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(The case of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the special case where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the SMoE function in Equation (<a href="#A1.E21" title="In A.1 Weight Space of Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Appendix A On the Weight Spaces of Mixture-of-Experts Architecture ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) simplifies to</p>
<table id="A3.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\mathcal{E}\left(x;\theta_{i}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(139)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the index <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by</p>
<table id="A3.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle i=\underset{i=1,\ldots,n}{\text{argmax}}\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mtext>argmax</mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle i=\underset{i=1,\ldots,n}{\text{argmax}}\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(140)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In this setting, the Top-<math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> gating mechanism selects only the expert with the highest score, and the softmax reduces to a one-hot distribution with a single nonzero entry equal to <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond the standard <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> symmetry acting on the expert parameters, the SMoE architecture with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> exhibits an additional, nontrivial invariance under the action of the multiplicative group <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, for any scalar <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\mathcal{S}\left(x;\left\{cW_{i},cb_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}\left(x;\left\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)=\mathcal{S}\left(x;\left\{cW_{i},cb_{i},\theta_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(141)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.2" class="ltx_p">as the <span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">argmax</span> used to select the active expert remains invariant under uniform positive scaling:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underset{i=1,\ldots,n}{\text{argmax}}\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)=\underset{i=1,\ldots,n}{\text{argmax}}\left(cW_{i}x+cb_{i}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mtext>argmax</mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mtext>argmax</mtext><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underset{i=1,\ldots,n}{\text{argmax}}\left(W_{i}x+b_{i}\right)=\underset{i=1,\ldots,n}{\text{argmax}}\left(cW_{i}x+cb_{i}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(142)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.3" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\Omega\left(\left\{W_{i},b_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, since only one expert is active at any given input, the architecture does not involve explicit interactions between experts. This leads to a more complex symmetry structure, including hidden and continuous transformations, which complicates theoretical analysis. For this reason, we exclude the case <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> from our main results and leave its investigation to future work.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Technical Details for Sections <a href="#S5" title="5 Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and  <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiments ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof for the Sufficiency of Permutation Invariance in LMC of MoE</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following result establishes that translation transformations do not affect the barrier loss between two parameter configurations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(c_{W},c_{b},\textup{id}_{n})\in G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>id</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(c_{W},c_{b},\textup{id}_{n})\in G(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{id}_{n}\in\textup{S}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>id</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{id}_{n}\in\textup{S}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the identity permutation. For any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{A},\phi_{B}\in\Phi(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{A},\phi_{B}\in\Phi(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, the barrier loss remains invariant under translation:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\phi_{A},\phi_{B})=B(\phi_{A},h\phi_{B})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\phi_{A},\phi_{B})=B(\phi_{A},h\phi_{B}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(143)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">That is, the translation components do not contribute to the barrier loss as defined in Equation (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Linear Mode Connectivity ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that</span></p>
<table id="A4.E144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(\phi_{A},\phi_{B})=\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\left[\mathcal{L}(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B})-\left(t\mathcal{L}(\phi_{A})+(1-t)\mathcal{L}(\phi_{B})\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(\phi_{A},\phi_{B})=\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\left[\mathcal{L}(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B})-\left(t\mathcal{L}(\phi_{A})+(1-t)\mathcal{L}(\phi_{B})\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(144)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, denote <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}=(tc_{W},tc_{b},\text{id}_{n})\in G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>id</mtext><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}=(tc_{W},tc_{b},\text{id}_{n})\in G(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{A},\phi_{B}\in\Phi(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{A},\phi_{B}\in\Phi(n)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx120" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi_{A}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E145.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(W^{A}_{i},b^{A}_{i},\theta^{A}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(W^{A}_{i},b^{A}_{i},\theta^{A}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(145)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi_{B}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E146.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(W^{B}_{i},b^{B}_{i},\theta^{B}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(W^{B}_{i},b^{B}_{i},\theta^{B}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(146)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx121" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t\phi_{A}+(1-t)(h\phi_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t\phi_{A}+(1-t)(h\phi_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=~" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=~</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t(W^{A}_{i},b^{A}_{i},\theta^{A}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}+(1-t)(W^{B}_{i}+c_{W},b^{B}_{i}+c_{b},\theta^{B}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t(W^{A}_{i},b^{A}_{i},\theta^{A}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}+(1-t)(W^{B}_{i}+c_{W},b^{B}_{i}+c_{b},\theta^{B}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=~" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=~</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big(tW^{A}_{i}+(1-t)W^{B}_{i}+(1-t)c_{W},tb^{A}_{i}+(1-t)b^{B}_{i}+(1-t)c_{b},t\theta^{A}_{i}+(1-t)\theta^{B}_{i}\big)_{i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big(tW^{A}_{i}+(1-t)W^{B}_{i}+(1-t)c_{W},tb^{A}_{i}+(1-t)b^{B}_{i}+(1-t)c_{b},t\theta^{A}_{i}+(1-t)\theta^{B}_{i}\big)_{i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=~" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=~</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E147.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big(h_{1-t}\big)\big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big(h_{1-t}\big)\big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(147)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since the group action of <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(n)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(n)</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the functionality of the MoE function <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx122" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;\phi_{B}\Big)=\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;h\phi_{B}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;\phi_{B}\Big)=\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;h\phi_{B}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(148)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx123" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;t\phi_{A}+(1-t)(h\phi_{B})\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;t\phi_{A}+(1-t)(h\phi_{B})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 70.0pt=\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;\big(h_{1-t}\big)\big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\big)\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="7.278em">=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 70.0pt=\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;\big(h_{1-t}\big)\big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\big)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 180.0pt=\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="18.278em">=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 180.0pt=\mathcal{D}\Big(\cdot;t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(149)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">These observations lead to</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx124" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\phi_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\phi_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E150.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}(h\phi_{B})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}(h\phi_{B}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(150)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E151"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}\Big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)(h\phi_{B})\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}\Big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)(h\phi_{B})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E151.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}\Big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}\Big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(151)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx125" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~B(\phi_{A},h\phi_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~B(\phi_{A},h\phi_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\Big[\mathcal{L}\big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)(h\phi_{B})\big)-\big(t\mathcal{L}(\phi_{A})+(1-t)\mathcal{L}(h\phi_{B})\big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\Big[\mathcal{L}\big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)(h\phi_{B})\big)-\big(t\mathcal{L}(\phi_{A})+(1-t)\mathcal{L}(h\phi_{B})\big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\Big[\mathcal{L}\big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\big)-\big(t\mathcal{L}(\phi_{A})+(1-t)\mathcal{L}(\phi_{B})\big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\Big[\mathcal{L}\big(t\phi_{A}+(1-t)\phi_{B}\big)-\big(t\mathcal{L}(\phi_{A})+(1-t)\mathcal{L}(\phi_{B})\big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E152.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~B(\phi_{A},\phi_{B})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~B(\phi_{A},\phi_{B}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(152)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the proof is finished.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof of the Permutation-Invariant Property for Equation (<a href="#S5.E11" title="In 5.2 Permutation Alignment Algorithm for Mixture-of-Experts ‣ 5 Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>)</h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The cost function defined in Method 2 of Section <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Permutation Alignment Algorithm for Mixture-of-Experts ‣ 5 Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> is permutation-invariant with respect to the hidden units of the experts in the MoE models.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each expert <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in the first Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> be the weight matrix and bias for the first layer, and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the weight matrix and bias for the second layer. Define the augmented matrices <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}_{i}=[A_{i},u_{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times(d+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}_{i}=[A_{i},u_{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times(d+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{i}=[B_{i},v_{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times(h+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{i}=[B_{i},v_{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times(h+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, for each expert <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> in the second MoE model <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the augmented matrices <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}^{\prime}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}^{\prime}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly. We define the Gram matrices <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+1)\times(d+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d+1)\times(d+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{i}(\widetilde{B}_{i})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{i}(\widetilde{B}_{i})^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> for each expert <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly for <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To establish permutation invariance, consider a permutation matrix <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times h}</annotation></semantics></math> applied to the hidden units of expert <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. For the first layer, the permuted augmented weight matrix is <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\widetilde{A}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\widetilde{A}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the second layer, the permutation affects the columns of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{i}=[B_{i},v_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{i}=[B_{i},v_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>, so the transformed matrix is <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>, leaving the bias <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged. We now verify the invariance of the Gram matrices under this permutation. For the first layer:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}(P\widetilde{A}_{i})=(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}P^{\top}P\widetilde{A}_{i}=(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}I\widetilde{A}_{i}=(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}(P\widetilde{A}_{i})=(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}P^{\top}P\widetilde{A}_{i}=(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}I\widetilde{A}_{i}=(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(153)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\top}P=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\top}P=I</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\times h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\times h</annotation></semantics></math> identity matrix. For the second layer:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx126" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\right)\left(\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\right)\left(\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}P&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\widetilde{B}_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>P</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}P&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\widetilde{B}_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}P&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\widetilde{B}_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}P^{\top}P&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\widetilde{B}_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\widetilde{B}_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{B}_{i}\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}\widetilde{B}_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widetilde{B}_{i}\widetilde{B}_{i}^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widetilde{B}_{i}\widetilde{B}_{i}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(154)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}I&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h+1)\times(h+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h+1)\times(h+1)</annotation></semantics></math> identity matrix. This confirms that both (<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{i}(\widetilde{B}_{i})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{i}(\widetilde{B}_{i})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> are invariant under permutations of the hidden units.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The cost matrix <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> for the Linear Assignment Problem (LAP) is <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{C_{i,j}\}_{1\leq i\leq n,1\leq j\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{C_{i,j}\}_{1\leq i\leq n,1\leq j\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A4.E155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i,j}=\left(\left\|(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}-(\widetilde{A}^{\prime}_{j})^{\top}\widetilde{A}^{\prime}_{j}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|\widetilde{B}_{i}(\widetilde{B}_{i})^{\top}-\widetilde{B}^{\prime}_{j}(\widetilde{B}^{\prime}_{j})^{\top}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i,j}=\left(\left\|(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}-(\widetilde{A}^{\prime}_{j})^{\top}\widetilde{A}^{\prime}_{j}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\left\|\widetilde{B}_{i}(\widetilde{B}_{i})^{\top}-\widetilde{B}^{\prime}_{j}(\widetilde{B}^{\prime}_{j})^{\top}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(155)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the Gram matrices <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widetilde{A}_{i})^{\top}\widetilde{A}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{i}(\widetilde{B}_{i})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{i}(\widetilde{B}_{i})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> (and their counterparts in <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) are permutation-invariant, their differences and the Frobenius norms of these differences are also invariant. Consequently, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> remains unchanged under permutations of the hidden units in either <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the cost function is permutation-invariant with respect to the hidden units of the experts, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Weight Matching Algorithm for Mixture-of-Experts</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> MoE model weights <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=(W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=(W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}=(W^{\prime}_{i},b^{\prime}_{i},\theta^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}=(W^{\prime}_{i},b^{\prime}_{i},\theta^{\prime}_{i})_{i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Permutation <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for experts, and permutations <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for hidden units

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             % Step 1: Match experts’ order using two methods

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> method in {gate, expert} <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Compute cost matrix <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Solve LAP to obtain expert permutation <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{method}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>method</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{method}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             % The two candidate expert orderings <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{gate}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{gate}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{expert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>expert</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{expert}}</annotation></semantics></math> are obtained

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             % Step 2: Align internal weights of matched expert pairs

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> method in {gate, expert} <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               Compute <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by applying Weight Matching to <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}_{\tau_{\text{method}}(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>method</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}_{\tau_{\text{method}}(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\tau_{\text{gate}},\left(\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)_{\text{gate}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mtext>gate</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\tau_{\text{gate}},\left(\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)_{\text{gate}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\tau_{\text{expert}},\left(\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)_{\text{expert}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>expert</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mtext>expert</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\tau_{\text{expert}},\left(\{P_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\right)_{\text{expert}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Weight Matching for Mixture-of-Experts</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Formal formulation of DeepSeekMoE</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we present the notation and formulations of three variants of MoE models: Dense MoE, Sparse MoE (SMoE), and DeepSeekMoE.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expert.</span> Given <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the input dimension. We define an <span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Expert</span> as a function <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta)\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta)\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, parameterized by <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>e</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{e}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of trainable parameters of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this work, we consider each expert <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\cdot;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> to be a feedforward neural network with ReLU activation functions. Unless stated otherwise, all experts are assumed to share the same architecture.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mixture of Expert with dense gating.</span> Given <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the number of experts, we define <em id="A4.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mixture-of-Experts with dense gating</em> as a function <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx127" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\big(x;\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\big)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\text{softmax}_{i}\big(s_{1}(x),\ldots,s_{n}(x)\big)\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}\big(x;\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\big)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\text{softmax}_{i}\big(s_{1}(x),\ldots,s_{n}(x)\big)\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(156)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}(x)=W_{i}x+b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}(x)=W_{i}x+b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> determines the contribution of each expert to the final output. Here, <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are the parameters of the <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> expert. The function <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=(s_{1},\ldots,s_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=(s_{1},\ldots,s_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is called the <span id="A4.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">gating score</span>, and is parameterized as <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\cdot;\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\cdot;\{W_{i},b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{i},b_{i})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{i},b_{i})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are the corresponding <span id="A4.SS4.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">gating</span> parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mixture-of-Experts with sparse gating. </span> Given a positive integer <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the number of activated experts, define the <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Top}\text{-}k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Top</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Top}\text{-}k</annotation></semantics></math> map by <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Top-}k(z)=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Top-}k(z)=\{i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{1},\ldots,i_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are the indices corresponding to the <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> largest components of <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. In the event of ties, we select smaller indices first. We define a <span id="A4.SS4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mixture-of-Experts with sparse gating</span> (SMoE) as a function <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. For <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(x)=\text{Top-}k(s(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(x)=\text{Top-}k(s(x))</annotation></semantics></math>, then define:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx128" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}\big(x;\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\big)=\sum_{i\in T(x)}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\Big(\big(s_{i}(x)\big)_{i\in T(x)}\Big)\cdot\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}\big(x;\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\big)=\sum_{i\in T(x)}\operatorname{softmax}_{i}\Big(\big(s_{i}(x)\big)_{i\in T(x)}\Big)\cdot\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(157)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">In other words, the Top-<math id="A4.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selects the <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> highest-scoring experts used to compute the output.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DeepseekMoE with shared and routed experts.</span> The DeepseekMoE architecture extends the sparse Mixture-of-Experts by incorporating both shared experts that are always active and routed experts that are sparsely activated based on the input. Given positive integers <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the number of shared and routed experts, respectively (<math id="A4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=n_{s}+n_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=n_{s}+n_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> as the total number of experts), and a positive integer <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{r}\leq n_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{r}\leq n_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the number of activated routed experts, the DeepseekMoE layer is defined as a function <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx129" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{M}\big(x;\{\theta_{i}^{(s)}\}_{i=1}^{n_{s}},\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n_{r}}\big)=\sum_{i=1}^{n_{s}}\mathcal{E}_{i}^{(s)}(x;\theta_{i}^{(s)})+\sum_{i=1}^{n_{r}}g_{i}(x)\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{i}^{(r)})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{M}\big(x;\{\theta_{i}^{(s)}\}_{i=1}^{n_{s}},\{W_{i},b_{i},\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n_{r}}\big)=\sum_{i=1}^{n_{s}}\mathcal{E}_{i}^{(s)}(x;\theta_{i}^{(s)})+\sum_{i=1}^{n_{r}}g_{i}(x)\mathcal{E}(x;\theta_{i}^{(r)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(158)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}^{(s)}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{(s)})\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}^{(s)}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{(s)})\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are the shared experts, parameterized by <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}^{(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}^{(s)}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{i}^{(r)}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{(r)})\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{i}^{(r)}(\cdot;\theta_{i}^{(r)})\colon\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are the routed experts, parameterized by <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The gating values <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> are computed as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx130" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{s}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{s}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{softmax}\big(s_{1}(x),\ldots,s_{n_{r}}(x)\big)\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{r}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{softmax}\big(s_{1}(x),\ldots,s_{n_{r}}(x)\big)\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{r}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\tilde{s}_{i}(x),&amp;\text{if }i\in\text{Top-}k_{r}(\tilde{s}(x))\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\tilde{s}_{i}(x),&amp;\text{if }i\in\text{Top-}k_{r}(\tilde{s}(x))\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">This formulation allows the model to leverage a combination of always-active shared experts and input-dependent routed experts, enhancing efficiency and performance in large-scale neural networks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Impact of Feedforward Reinitialization on Pretrained Transformer Performance</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We empirically investigate the sensitivity of pretrained Transformer models to targeted parameter reinitialization within their Feedforward Network (FFN) modules. The FFN, a critical component for non-linear transformations and feature representation within each Transformer block, was selectively reinitialized layer by layer to assess its functional contribution and the robustness of the overall model architecture. This analysis aims to identify the extent to which performance is dependent on the learned parameters of individual FFNs and to potentially highlight layers that are more critical to maintaining task proficiency. To this end, experiments were conducted on two representative model-task pairs:</p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Image Classification using a Vision Transformer (ViT-Base, patch size 16, image resolution 224) pretrained on ImageNet.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Language Modeling using a GPT-2 model (12-layer, hidden size 768) pretrained on WikiText103.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each model, the parameters of the FFN subcomponent within a single Transformer block were reinitialized using a standard initialization scheme (e.g., variance scaling), while all other model parameters, including attention weights and the FFNs in other layers, were kept frozen from the pretrained state. Following reinitialization, the models were evaluated on their respective tasks without any subsequent fine-tuning. This approach isolates the immediate effect of disrupting a single FFN on pretrained performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix E Impact of Feedforward Reinitialization on Pretrained Transformer Performance ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#A5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix E Impact of Feedforward Reinitialization on Pretrained Transformer Performance ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> illustrate the performance degradation observed when reinitializing the FFN at different layers for the ViT and GPT-2 models, respectively. A striking observation is the significantly larger performance drop (increase in loss, decrease in accuracy) when reinitializing the FFN in the first layer (Layer 0) compared to any subsequent layer. While reinitializing FFNs in layers beyond the first does result in performance degradation, this impact is markedly less severe than at Layer 0. The results further reveal a non-uniform sensitivity profile among these subsequent layers, with FFN reinitialization in middle layers tending to induce a more pronounced performance decrement than in later layers. This pattern suggests a unique functional importance or sensitivity associated with the initial layer’s FFN, while the network’s architecture, particularly the presence of skip connections, appears to enable a greater degree of resilience to disruption in FFNs at deeper layers.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11348v1/imagenet_layer_metric.svg" id="A5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/199;" width="476" height="199"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Performance degradation in ViT-Base on ImageNet due to FFN reinitialization at different layers.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11348v1/wikitext103_layer_metric.svg" id="A5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/199;" width="476" height="199"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Effect of FFN reinitialization on GPT-2 perplexity across layers on WikiText103.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A key observation from these experiments, particularly for deeper and more complex models with skip connections, is that reinitializing a single FFN (except potentially the very first one) often does not lead to a catastrophic performance collapse. This phenomenon can be partially attributed to the presence of skip connections, which facilitate the unimpeded flow of information across layers, allowing features learned by other parts of the network to bypass the disrupted FFN. Furthermore, standard weight initialization schemes typically employ relatively small scales centered around zero, meaning the reinitialized FFN parameters introduce a perturbation that is initially small and balanced compared to the potentially large and specialized weights learned during pretraining. This combination of architectural properties (skip connections) and initialization characteristics helps the model maintain functionality, suggesting that the reinitialized state may remain within or close to the original optimization basin found during pretraining. Previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite> has highlighted how skip connections contribute to flatter minima and improve training stability in deep networks, which aligns with the observation that reinitialization causes less disruption than might intuitively be expected.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To further investigate the generality of this observation, we also conducted FFN reinitialization experiments on tasks commonly used for evaluating model robustness and optimization landscape properties, including text classification tasks (IMDB Review <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite>, AGNEWS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">86</a>]</cite>, DBPedia <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>) and additional language modeling tasks (EnWik8 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, Penn Treebank (Word Level) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>). Table <a href="#A5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix E Impact of Feedforward Reinitialization on Pretrained Transformer Performance ‣ On Linear Mode Connectivity of Mixture-of-Experts Architectures" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presents a summary of the performance changes on these datasets after reinitializing an arbitrary single FFN layer compared to the original pretrained performance, and also shows performance after subsequent fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Effect of single FFN reinitialization on various tasks. "Pretrained" indicates performance of the original model. "Reinitialize" shows performance after reinitializing a single FFN layer. "Finetune" shows performance after fine-tuning the reinitialized model. "Naive Loss Barrier" refers to the loss barrier observed between two fine-tuned models initialized with different random seeds and trained with different batch orders.</figcaption>
